# --- secrets -------------------------------------------------------------- #
# The API key lives in .env, which is never committed. .env.example documents
# the variable names with empty values.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# --- scratch --------------------------------------------------------------- #
# Transfer and setup artefacts, editor leftovers, archives. None of these are
# part of the submission; they exist only to move the tree onto a machine.
finalise.sh
*.tar.gz
*.patch
*.orig
*.rej

# The task brief itself. It is Sarvam's document, not part of this submission,
# and republishing someone else's brief on a public repository is not a
# decision this repository should make quietly. Keep it locally; do not upload.
Kivi_Backend_Full_Stack_Task_Clean_Cover.pdf

# --- generated at runtime -------------------------------------------------- #
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
*.egg-info/
# Anchored, and it has to be. Unanchored, `data/` matches a directory of that
# name at ANY depth, which silently excluded `evals/data/` (every fixture, the
# seed persona, the derived tier) and `src/psm/data/` (the common-word list) -
# so a fresh clone had no evaluation and no guard vocabulary, and the first
# command a reviewer runs failed. The runtime database is the only `data/` that
# should ever be ignored, and it lives at the repository root.
/data/
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# --- what is NOT ignored, and why ------------------------------------------ #
# evals/results/ IS committed. The brief asks for generated evaluation results
# as part of the submission, and a claim in the README that cannot be checked
# against the run that produced it is not evidence. Everything under it is
# regenerable with `make eval` and `make explore`.
#
# evals/cassettes/ IS committed, as an empty directory with a .gitkeep. What
# makes the evaluation runnable without an API key is that it makes zero model
# calls at all: the default `llm.stub` abstains and the default formatter is a
# passthrough. Cassettes exist for the optional `--replay` path only, nothing
# is recorded into them, and `--replay` therefore fails with `CassetteMiss` by
# design rather than appearing to pass on nothing.
#
# evals/data/ and src/psm/data/ ARE committed. See the note on `/data/` above.
